hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1389","Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The sun was eclipsed. One day during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up to pray, and he stood until he could barely bow, then He bowed until he could hardly raise his head, then he raised his head and could hardly prostrate, then he prostrated and could barely raise his head, then he raised his head but could hardly He prostrated, then he prostrated and could hardly raise his head.”"
